# Rules the spec declares that no Go comment cites — the ratchet half of
# scripts/rule-citations.sh. One rule per line: the id, then a reason.
#
# THE LIST MAY ONLY SHRINK. Cite a rule and its line goes; the script fails on a
# listed rule that has since been cited, so the list cannot rot into a permanent
# exemption that silences the "uncited and unlisted" failure. It started at 48
# entries; sd-924c13's sweep bound the verification family to code and took 16
# of them, which is the mechanism working.
#
# What a reason says, and it says one of these three:
#
#   another layer's  — the rule governs something this library never does. It
#                      stands as long as that holds.
#   citation owed    — this library enforces the rule and no comment says so. The
#                      line names the site, so the citation lands where the rule
#                      is enforced rather than anywhere convenient.
#   nothing to cite  — the rule is unimplemented here, so there is no site. The
#                      line goes when the check does, not before.
#
# A reason that says only "not yet" says none of that: it neither justifies the
# exemption nor names what removes it.

# Access — accounts, targets, and the letters they hold. Grants are server
# configuration resolved before a call reaches the library, which sees only the
# constraints it is handed (Constraints, contribution.go).
R-AGRANT       another layer's: grants and accounts are the server's configuration
R-ABRANCH      another layer's: per-branch rights are checked before the library is called
R-ATABLE       another layer's: rights over $branches are the server's to check
R-AUNIVERSE    another layer's: the privileged $universe read is the server's to grant
R-ABOOKMARK    another layer's: no access grant covers a 𝒰_hist write, so there is none to check here

# Contribution rules — the six-step procedure, whose write path is the Sequencer
# in adapter/sequencer.
R-C1BASE       citation owed: base (k, t) at open, adapter/sequencer
R-C2DATE       citation owed: no claim dated after the base time, adapter/sequencer
R-C3CLOSE      citation owed: closing over references, contribution.go
R-C4KEY        citation owed: claim dated inside its key's window, verify.go ruleKeyWindow
R-C4SEAL       citation owed: sealed once verified, adapter/sequencer
R-C5PERSIST    citation owed: closure durable before the merge, adapter/sequencer
R-C6SIGN       citation owed: Sequencer claims name its own contributor, adapter/sequencer

# Field syntax.

# RQL — the query type and the native engine that is the conformance oracle.
R-QEVAL        citation owed: fixed evaluation order, query.go
R-QFORM        citation owed: original or materialized field values, query.go

# Translation to Cypher — the neo4j backend's own chapter.
R-QCSTEP       citation owed: a step as a variable-length segment, adapter/storage/neo4j
